Z||000000||TheHans||01-23-2001||01:40 AM||||My 85 duke...<BR>Looks pretty bad.<BR>Ready to flatline...<BR>I've got severe dirt and -whoknowswhat<BR>on the middle counsel and the door handles<BR>Can't get it off for the life of me.<BR>Anyone have the secret weapon?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfixit58||01-23-2001||07:47 AM||||For those really tough stains that your typical cleaners wont remove, I've used GoJo Orange and a rag with great success. <P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||bHooper||01-23-2001||09:13 AM||||409!  the blue stuff.||||reg||1
Z||000003||fiero56||01-23-2001||11:50 AM||||Simple Green seems to work well for me. I've never used it on vinyl though, might want to check the lable before putting any on.||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||01-23-2001||12:42 PM||||I use Greased Ligntning by the jug, you can mix it with water as mild or strong as you want.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Raydar||01-23-2001||01:12 PM||||Mean Green. Available at Dollar General. Have never seen it anywhere else. Test it on something "hidden" before you use it. Worked better for me than Simple Green. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000006||286SE'S||01-23-2001||04:28 PM||||I took my door handles off and put them in the sink. Tried all the cleaners under the sink and finally used the cleanser (ajax) and that took off all the grease and marks. It did leave the finish a little dull so had to use some armor-all to shine it up. Also put a little cleanser on a rag and got the shoe marks off the door sills and gunk on the center console. When the spray stuff fails a little gritty cleanser is worth a try.||||reg||1
Z||000007||LarryB||01-23-2001||05:22 PM||||I removed my console and used an old toothbrush, SoftScrub, and water to thin it out, then used damp paper towels to wipe the stuff off before it could try up.  I did basically the same thing with the door sides and handles, they came out great. Took about a half-hour for the console and ~ 15 minutes per door. <P>Gotta be careful using stuff like ArmorAll because it attracts dirt and other gunk. ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Tina||01-23-2001||06:18 PM||||Try'd everything underneath the <BR>kitchen sink.<BR>My alltime favorites.<P>1.Scrubbing Bubbles Bathroom Cleaner<BR>2.Huggies Baby wipes  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||MikeSchaefer||01-23-2001||06:28 PM||||At body-shop supply stores, you can get special vinyl-cleaning products and a product called vinyl conditioner.  Use them consecutively and I bet it'll come right off. <BR>Mike Schaefer <A HREF="http://surf.to/fiero" TARGET=_blank>http://surf.to/fiero</A> ||||reg||6
